MoonWren is an independent MoonBit implementation of the Wren language. The
public language documentation and compatibility behavior of Wren are used as
references. Selected unmodified Wren 0.4.0 test inputs under
conformance/wren-0.4.0 are included for differential testing.

Wren is available at https://github.com/wren-lang/wren and is distributed
under the MIT License by Robert Nystrom and contributors.
The complete upstream copyright and permission notice is reproduced in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/Wren-LICENSE.txt and applies to the unmodified upstream
test inputs and to portions adapted from the Wren 0.4.0 reference project.

The built-in `random` and `meta` optional modules reproduce the public API and
algorithms of Wren 0.4.0's optional modules. Their MoonBit implementation is
adapted from that MIT-licensed reference behavior.

The command-line package depends on moonbitlang/x, distributed under the
Apache License 2.0 by the MoonBit project contributors.
